{
  "dom_id": "step-7778",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Completing a Statement Describing a Ratio as a Fraction",
  "problem": "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nTo make a fertilizer Esther mixed $2$ quarts of fertilizer concentrate and $3$ quarts of distilled water, so there are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133630/assets/e67bc79fa98ba44b9b1c5d5727182e936472f4b7d7b52967a54b069f178cf66d.svg) quarts of fertilizer concentrate for each quart of distilled water.",
  "worked_solution": "The ratio of the number of quarts of fertilizer concentrate to the number of quarts of distilled water is  ${\\color{blue}{2}}:{\\color{red}{3}}.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}{2}}}{{\\color{red}{3}}}\n$$\n\nThis means that there is $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ quart of fertilizer concentrate for each quart of distilled water.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
